urname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Jackson</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Caspi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Good test-retest reliability for standard and advanced false-belief tasks across a wide range of abilities</article-title><source>J Child Psychol Psychiatry</source><year>2000</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>483</fpage><lpage>490</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10836678</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Happ&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Frith</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Theory of mind and social impairment in children with conduct disorder</article-title><source>Br J Dev Psychol</source><year>1996</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>385</fpage><lpage>398</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sutton</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Reeves</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Keogh</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Disruptive behaviour, avoidance of responsibilityy and theory of mind</article-title><source>Br J Dev Psychol</source><year>2000</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>12</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Association</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name></person-group><source>Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders 4th edition, text revision</source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>Washington DC: American Psychiatric Association</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group p